WEBVTT

00:23.880 --> 00:28.630
I LOOKED AT THE BLOOMING
FLOWERS IN MY SHINING DREAM

00:28.800 --> 00:32.350
<i>NO MORE LIFE</i>
I WAS OBSESSED

00:32.520 --> 00:35.110
MY PAST WAS SCATTERED

00:35.280 --> 00:38.670
<i>JEALOUS</i>, <i>JEALOUS</i>
BY THOSE HANDS

00:38.840 --> 00:41.990
<i>JEALOUS</i>, <i>JEALOUS</i>
I WAS CALLED

00:42.160 --> 00:45.310
<i>JEALOUS</i>, <i>JEALOUS</i>
BY A LIGHT SHINING

00:45.480 --> 00:48.710
<i>JEALOUS</i>, <i>JEALOUS</i>
IN THE DARKNESS

00:48.880 --> 00:52.320
<i>ONE MORE TIME</i>
IN THE TWINKLING LIGHT

00:52.480 --> 00:55.440
WATCH THAT FIGURE FADE AWAY

00:55.600 --> 00:59.230
<i>NO MORE LIFE</i>
I WAS LEFT BEHIND

00:59.400 --> 01:02.150
BUT TOMORROW WE'LL MEET AGAIN

01:02.320 --> 01:05.440
<i>JEALOUS</i>, <i>JEALOUS</i>
BY THOSE HANDS

01:05.600 --> 01:08.750
<i>JEALOUS</i>, <i>JEALOUS</i>
I WAS CALLED

01:08.920 --> 01:12.150
<i>JEALOUS</i>, <i>JEALOUS</i>
BY A LIGHT SHINING

01:12.320 --> 01:15.470
<i>JEALOUS</i>, <i>JEALOUS</i>
IN THE DARKNESS

01:15.640 --> 01:21.400
SURROUNDED BY THE LIGHT

01:21.560 --> 01:23.840
<i>DON'T CLOSE EYES
HELP ME</i>

01:24.000 --> 01:29.330
WHEN I SCREAM
<i>WILL BE SATISFACTION, YOU KNOW</i>

01:32.820 --> 01:37.040
The seventh month of 1600 AD, or Keicho 5.

01:37.410 --> 01:41.210
Charging Tokugawa Ieyasu with thirteen articles of impeachment,

01:41.210 --> 01:48.130
Ishida Mitsunari sent messengers to various daimyo in the name of the Toyotomi clan,

01:48.130 --> 01:51.300
telling them to raise armies.

01:51.300 --> 01:56.390
At the same time, beings seeking to end the period of turbulence

01:56.390 --> 02:00.270
and build a kingdom to last a thousand years

02:00.270 --> 02:04.520
were about to awaken from a thousand-year sleep.

02:04.520 --> 02:06.520
And then...

02:06.520 --> 02:10.280
On the fifteenth day of the ninth month, at Sekigahara,

02:10.280 --> 02:12.740
the Eastern Army of Tokugawa Ieyasu clashed with

02:12.740 --> 02:17.870
the Western Army of the Toyotomi clan and Ishida Mitsunari.

02:17.870 --> 02:21.330
As a result of the performance of Kobayakawa Hideaki's troops,

02:21.330 --> 02:27.250
the Western Army of the Toyotomi clan and
Ishida Mitsunari achieved a sweeping victory,

02:27.250 --> 02:33.510
bringing what should have been
three hundred years of peace to the world.

02:34.340 --> 02:39.390
You should all be quite familiar with this story...

02:44.360 --> 02:49.230
In order to find the seven artifacts that
can be used to imprison the ayakashi...

02:49.440 --> 02:57.150
Musashi, Ronin, Ninjataro
and Princess Yume went east.

02:57.880 --> 03:02.990
I, Danjo and Sasuke Sarutobi went west.

03:04.080 --> 03:09.950
Musashi and his companions arrived
at one of the castles containing an artifact...

03:10.120 --> 03:15.160
but the castle turned out
to be at the bottom of a lake.

03:16.080 --> 03:21.080
Musashi and Ronin dove
in towards the castle...

03:21.520 --> 03:26.950
and after defeating the shikigami, they
managed to get their hands on an artifact.

03:27.880 --> 03:29.080
However...

03:29.600 --> 03:34.310
Musashi was attacked
by a mechanical puppet.

03:34.960 --> 03:37.920
The puppet is the latest invention of...

03:38.080 --> 03:43.880
Dabinoji, built at the
request of Yasha: <i>Rasetsu</i>.

03:47.060 --> 03:49.840
THAT WOMAN AGAIN

03:57.280 --> 03:58.480
Go for it.

04:03.600 --> 04:05.560
Are you okay, Musashi?

04:05.720 --> 04:07.150
More or less.

04:07.600 --> 04:08.950
You've been tricked.

04:10.840 --> 04:12.190
Totally.

05:47.520 --> 05:49.590
We had finally gotten our hands on it!

05:50.640 --> 05:52.550
What about the mechanical puppet?

05:52.760 --> 05:54.720
It disappeared in the wild.

05:55.240 --> 05:58.840
It was neither an ayakashi nor a shikigami.

05:59.000 --> 06:01.510
A mechanical puppet... impossible!

06:03.600 --> 06:07.200
There's no doubt, old Dabinoji built it!

06:07.560 --> 06:12.630
But Mr. Dabinoji was supposed
to be one of your friends.

06:12.800 --> 06:15.070
- Why did he do that?
- I don't know.

06:35.640 --> 06:37.040
You're back.

06:51.760 --> 06:55.520
Is it true that he brought back the first artifact?

06:59.560 --> 07:01.440
Take a look for yourself!

07:06.000 --> 07:07.830
Is this an artifact?

07:08.000 --> 07:11.550
You are a genius, Mr. da Vinci. Congratulations.

07:15.320 --> 07:18.760
Are you putting all seven artifacts in here?

07:19.200 --> 07:20.840
Exactly.

07:21.320 --> 07:24.040
And what happens when you have all seven?

07:24.200 --> 07:26.190
Yeah, what happens?

07:28.200 --> 07:29.920
Nothing happens.

07:31.400 --> 07:36.110
What do you mean? Nothing
happens? That's not fun at all.

07:36.840 --> 07:41.720
However, if the humans get
the seven artifacts instead...

07:41.880 --> 07:46.240
they will be able to imprison
the ayakashi for eternity.

07:46.400 --> 07:48.600
Including you, Lord Ryogen.

07:48.800 --> 07:50.710
That would bore me!

07:51.400 --> 07:56.760
That's why Mr. da Vinci
and Shingen Takeda...

07:56.920 --> 07:59.360
are helping us get them
before the humans.

07:59.920 --> 08:05.000
We want to get them before Musashi.

08:05.680 --> 08:07.000
So that's how it is.

08:07.160 --> 08:11.950
I'm counting on you.
We need to find the second artifact!

08:15.480 --> 08:18.200
Where are you going, Lord Ryogen?

08:18.640 --> 08:21.760
Young girls are waiting for me at the top.

08:22.880 --> 08:26.710
Without youth essence,
I will lose my soft skin.

08:26.920 --> 08:29.720
I'm counting on you for the rest!

08:34.240 --> 08:36.150
I apologize for that.

08:36.360 --> 08:41.800
Lord Ryogen relies on you
completely, Mr. da Vinci.

08:43.120 --> 08:46.720
You're wrong, he's counting on you.

08:52.160 --> 08:53.750
However, Yasha...

08:53.920 --> 08:57.280
he's still leyasu Tokugawa,
even rotten as he is.

08:57.480 --> 09:00.840
Underestimating him is a big risk.

09:03.960 --> 09:06.790
I appreciate your advice.

09:07.320 --> 09:11.310
How are we going to
get the second artifact?

09:11.720 --> 09:14.470
We can use Rasetsu again.

09:14.960 --> 09:16.840
I'd rather not.

09:17.000 --> 09:24.920
The next castle is full of
traps set by a Yin-Yang monk.

09:25.080 --> 09:30.480
Seeing how Musashi handles
that will be interesting.

09:32.320 --> 09:38.240
And the artifact he worked so hard to
obtain will be promptly snatched from him.

09:38.640 --> 09:40.550
Exactly.

09:41.400 --> 09:42.630
It's cowardly.

09:45.480 --> 09:47.520
I like this strategy.

09:55.160 --> 09:58.310
Danjo, Sasuke, are we leaving now?

09:58.520 --> 09:59.720
Yes.

09:59.760 --> 10:04.280
Princess Kaguya!
Your Highness! I beg you to wait!

10:04.880 --> 10:09.160
Mitsunari Ishida.
He saw through our actions.

10:09.320 --> 10:12.230
Let's hurry before he catches us.

10:12.440 --> 10:13.870
Still...

10:14.040 --> 10:19.880
He's gonna tell us the search for the
artifact is dangerous and that he opposes it.

10:20.400 --> 10:24.550
I am also of the opinion
that this trip is dangerous.

10:25.080 --> 10:29.310
We cannot impose this burden
on Musashi and Yume alone.

10:29.520 --> 10:32.160
I agree, but...

10:50.400 --> 10:52.870
Sasuke, please do it.

10:53.040 --> 10:54.240
You can count on me!

10:57.280 --> 10:59.430
Ninja Art: Metamorphosis!

11:00.320 --> 11:02.150
What, two Princess Kaguyas?

11:02.720 --> 11:05.080
You're skilled, Sasuke.

11:05.240 --> 11:07.600
I am honored by your compliments!

11:08.200 --> 11:11.560
How long have you mastered ninja arts for?

11:13.000 --> 11:16.120
Sorry, I sometimes scream like a monkey.

11:16.280 --> 11:19.240
Yes, I've been a good ninja since childhood.

11:19.440 --> 11:26.320
Sasuke Sarutobi of Sanada Ten Braves has
always had the reputation of being a genius ninja!

11:27.160 --> 11:29.830
Both of you head west.

11:30.000 --> 11:31.880
I will follow you soon.

11:32.040 --> 11:33.710
Thank you very much.

11:48.720 --> 11:50.200
Princess Kaguya!

11:50.920 --> 11:54.470
Lord Mitsunari, what's with all the fuss?

11:56.680 --> 12:03.400
Well, I wanted to prevent you from
going on a quest for artifacts... Here?

12:04.080 --> 12:05.400
What's the matter?

12:05.920 --> 12:08.120
So you didn't go?

12:08.920 --> 12:12.120
Did you think I would undertake such a journey?

12:13.880 --> 12:18.760
Only Danjo and Sasuke Sarutobi
of Sanada Ten Braves went.

12:18.920 --> 12:21.230
I just came by to greet them.

12:22.400 --> 12:23.910
Now I understand!

12:24.440 --> 12:26.590
Now let's go back to the castle.

12:33.680 --> 12:35.190
It's nothing.

12:36.320 --> 12:37.800
I understand.

12:46.120 --> 12:48.760
Princess Kaguya, I will join you soon!

12:59.560 --> 13:02.360
Musashi seems frustrated.

13:05.120 --> 13:10.160
It seems that having the artifact
stolen is really eating away at him.

13:10.720 --> 13:12.360
Let's cheer him up!

13:13.000 --> 13:15.360
Ninjaichiro, go for it.

13:19.160 --> 13:20.510
Hey, Ninjajuro!

13:21.000 --> 13:25.670
It's not <i>ichiro</i>, <i>juro</i>, <i>jiro</i> or <i>happyakurokujuhachigo</i>!

13:26.160 --> 13:28.600
I'm tired of this joke!

13:29.280 --> 13:30.600
You're no fun.

13:31.320 --> 13:35.710
Besides, you have been
his friend for a long time!

13:35.880 --> 13:37.840
It's up to you to help him.

13:38.880 --> 13:40.080
Friend?

13:40.600 --> 13:43.830
Don't use that word lightly!

13:44.960 --> 13:47.600
Besides, we haven't always been friends.

13:50.600 --> 13:52.080
How was it like before?

13:52.240 --> 13:53.910
We used to be enemies.

13:54.440 --> 13:55.670
I didn't know that!

13:56.640 --> 13:58.630
That's in the past.

13:59.560 --> 14:01.390
Yume, please...

14:02.160 --> 14:03.880
Me?

14:04.080 --> 14:05.720
Please do so.

14:06.240 --> 14:07.670
I understand.

14:11.520 --> 14:12.750
Musashi.

14:14.480 --> 14:17.680
I'm sorry about the first artifact.

14:17.840 --> 14:24.230
But you have to bounce back and think
about the second and third artifacts...

14:26.280 --> 14:29.530
- What's it?
- I'll have <i>hoto</i> noodle soup!

14:30.880 --> 14:35.480
Since earlier, I was wondering
what I was going to eat.

14:35.640 --> 14:40.880
But since this is the country of Kai,
we might as well take eat a local specialty!

14:42.800 --> 14:44.360
This place looks good!

14:45.040 --> 14:48.510
Was it lunch you were worried about?

14:49.320 --> 14:51.360
What else?

14:51.960 --> 14:53.160
Nothing...

14:53.560 --> 14:56.310
I'm starving!

15:00.960 --> 15:02.520
Let's go inside too.

15:08.880 --> 15:11.320
Musashi, I finally found you.

15:16.200 --> 15:17.430
It's so good!

15:18.160 --> 15:20.720
It's the best dish around!

15:21.440 --> 15:25.430
What's wrong with you all?
Eat before it gets cold.

15:25.840 --> 15:27.040
Musashi.

15:27.280 --> 15:28.480
Yes?

15:28.880 --> 15:30.600
Aren't you frustrated?

15:31.400 --> 15:32.880
About the artifact?

15:34.800 --> 15:37.080
Of course I am.

15:37.240 --> 15:40.280
It doesn't seem to affect your appetite.

15:40.440 --> 15:41.640
Is that bad?

15:41.720 --> 15:42.990
I didn't say that.

15:43.440 --> 15:46.430
Beating myself up won't change anything.

15:46.600 --> 15:49.960
Frustration will not give us the artifact back.

15:50.120 --> 15:52.480
First of all, we have to fill our bellies.

15:53.400 --> 15:56.950
You're right, I agree with you there.
That is so you.

15:57.400 --> 15:59.310
You are amazing!

15:59.480 --> 16:01.760
I admire your attitude!

16:02.320 --> 16:05.230
It sounded like you were being ironic.

16:05.400 --> 16:07.440
Not at all!

16:08.360 --> 16:12.190
Anyway, I'm glad you're
not feeling down.

16:12.360 --> 16:13.760
Come on, let's eat.

16:14.240 --> 16:15.440
Yeah.

16:15.800 --> 16:17.310
Bon appétit!

16:23.480 --> 16:24.750
Desperado!

16:24.960 --> 16:26.710
I've been looking for you!

16:26.920 --> 16:29.310
You don't give up!

16:29.480 --> 16:32.470
Unless an ayakashi is
manipulating you again.

16:32.680 --> 16:35.320
Look, the failed ninja is here too.

16:35.520 --> 16:37.270
What do you mean, "failed"?

16:37.480 --> 16:38.750
Failed?

16:39.240 --> 16:41.830
You're a failure, so I called you a failure.

16:42.000 --> 16:43.270
That's rude!

16:43.960 --> 16:47.080
Calm down, Ninjasaburo!
It's true, you're a failure.

16:47.280 --> 16:48.510
Master Musashi!

16:48.720 --> 16:51.160
Are those Japanese noodles?

16:52.040 --> 16:55.240
Manager, do you have a fork? No?

16:59.760 --> 17:03.830
What's wrong with you? You don't
want to kill Musashi anymore?

17:04.040 --> 17:06.160
I've been thinking about this.

17:06.320 --> 17:09.470
He saved my life the last time.

17:10.640 --> 17:12.470
Yes, sort of.

17:12.680 --> 17:17.440
That's not the reason,
but I do want a ceasefire.

17:18.080 --> 17:19.430
Thank you.

17:22.280 --> 17:24.480
- What is that?
- Open it.

17:28.160 --> 17:30.070
These are...

17:30.920 --> 17:34.960
He told me they were bullets
designed for the demon gun.

17:35.120 --> 17:36.550
Really?

17:37.000 --> 17:39.990
Master Takuan asked me to give them to you.

17:40.160 --> 17:42.800
I am also indebted to him.

17:42.960 --> 17:47.190
That's why I followed you here.

17:48.080 --> 17:50.470
Is this from Master Takuan?

17:52.880 --> 17:56.950
Like the flammable bullets
you bought from Dabinoji,

17:57.120 --> 18:01.640
those bullets have
unlimited uses once loaded.

18:02.040 --> 18:07.430
There are three different ones,
each with a different power and ability.

18:09.800 --> 18:11.870
Can I really have them?

18:12.680 --> 18:15.560
Is Master Takuan still in good health?

18:15.720 --> 18:19.840
He said he was going on a trip to a distant country.

18:20.040 --> 18:22.240
- Where?
- Who knows?

18:23.000 --> 18:29.190
I have completed my task.
I will kill my father's killer next time.

18:29.840 --> 18:32.450
I really didn't kill your father!
Stop with this!

18:34.840 --> 18:36.040
Desperado!

18:37.920 --> 18:42.310
Wouldn't you like to
join us in our quest?

18:43.960 --> 18:46.030
Yume, just a minute!

18:46.200 --> 18:50.480
This woman is after Musashi's life!

18:51.240 --> 18:53.440
And for a false accusation!

18:54.000 --> 18:55.270
Everything will be fine.

18:55.440 --> 18:59.070
She is also an important
person who will help you.

19:00.440 --> 19:04.070
But who are you?
And how do you know me?

19:04.800 --> 19:09.030
I know everything about you
because I saw you in a dream.

19:09.680 --> 19:12.750
In a dream?
Is the little girl feeling well?

19:13.560 --> 19:15.760
I'll explain later.

19:16.560 --> 19:18.550
Anyway, I'm against it.

19:18.760 --> 19:19.960
We have to.

19:20.080 --> 19:23.360
Miss Desperado must accompany us.

19:23.920 --> 19:25.190
Do you agree?

19:40.800 --> 19:43.630
This is where the second artifact is located?

19:52.240 --> 19:56.920
It's strange. It's in this castle, for sure.

19:57.080 --> 20:00.040
But I don't have its exact location.

20:02.440 --> 20:05.670
We just have to split up and look for it.

20:06.600 --> 20:09.960
Fortunately, there is no sign of ayakashi.

20:26.640 --> 20:29.440
It looks like there is no shikigami either.

20:29.600 --> 20:31.560
Looks like it.

20:32.320 --> 20:33.990
But let's not get too excited.

20:34.960 --> 20:38.430
The Yin-Yang monks probably
prepared something very dangerous.

20:38.600 --> 20:41.830
We'll deal with it when it comes.
Let's split up and search!

20:45.360 --> 20:47.000
I'll go that way.

20:47.160 --> 20:49.470
Then I'll go this way.

20:49.640 --> 20:52.440
Desperado, go with Yume.

20:52.920 --> 20:56.470
Why should I help Musashi?

21:04.520 --> 21:08.960
Forgive me for bringing you
along, Miss Desperado.

21:09.720 --> 21:14.030
But you're an important
person, so please...

21:14.200 --> 21:17.000
It's okay, I'll do it.

21:17.160 --> 21:19.910
Stop looking at me
with those teary eyes.

21:20.120 --> 21:23.080
I'm a woman, after all.

21:23.240 --> 21:27.470
Pretend I didn't say anything.
Stay close to me.

21:27.640 --> 21:28.840
Okay.

21:55.520 --> 21:58.720
Damn! An Yin-Yang monk trap?

22:05.440 --> 22:06.640
Who is there?

22:22.480 --> 22:24.390
Where is the light?
Where is the exit?

22:30.920 --> 22:32.560
What is this room?

22:33.280 --> 22:36.080
It looks like we're not alone.

22:37.520 --> 22:41.350
It seems so.
Princess, stay close to me!

22:52.120 --> 22:53.440
I know...

22:53.640 --> 22:55.070
you're there!

23:09.560 --> 23:10.760
What the...

23:27.560 --> 23:28.960
Who are you?

23:34.680 --> 23:35.880
It can't be...

23:36.080 --> 23:37.710
The past me?

23:38.040 --> 23:39.240
Impossible!

23:39.480 --> 23:43.270
Are you an impostor disguised as me?

23:44.520 --> 23:47.910
No, I used to be you!

23:48.520 --> 23:50.510
Used to be?

23:51.040 --> 23:52.680
What's going on?

24:25.360 --> 24:27.160
THROUGH THE CROWDS

24:27.320 --> 24:31.080
THEY'RE CUTTING OFF YOUR ESCAPE

24:31.240 --> 24:34.950
IN THIS TWILIGHT TOWN
I HEAR PIERCING SOUNDS

24:35.120 --> 24:38.880
LIKE A WANDERING CAT

24:39.040 --> 24:40.790
WITHOUT KNOWING

24:40.960 --> 24:42.760
WHERE TO GO

24:42.920 --> 24:46.680
I'M TRAPPED IN THIS TOWN THAT NEVER SLEEPS

24:46.840 --> 24:50.360
MY REFLECTION IN THE MIRROR

24:50.520 --> 24:55.200
SEEING MYSELF TRANSFORM

24:55.360 --> 24:57.720
I'M HOLDING ON

24:57.880 --> 25:01.160
FOR AS LONG AS POSSIBLE

25:03.200 --> 25:07.830
I'LL SHOW YOU THAT I CAN

25:08.000 --> 25:10.560
WIN OVER THIS TOWN

25:11.720 --> 25:13.760
FROM MY BURNING HEART

25:13.920 --> 25:15.910
SHINE SO MANY

25:16.080 --> 25:19.870
DAZZLING COLORS AND LIGHTS

25:20.040 --> 25:21.550
FLOODING ALL OVER

25:21.720 --> 25:23.710
SCATTERING ALL OVER

25:23.880 --> 25:27.030
SURROUNDING ME

25:27.200 --> 25:29.650
SOLEMNLY

25:31.420 --> 25:35.250
I will get my hands on
the second artifact!

25:35.420 --> 25:38.090
But why must I fight the past me?

25:38.980 --> 25:42.130
The next chapter: <i>Shoot the Past</i>!
